Sir Mark,

I attach a formal request to the Metropolitan Police Service, addressed to =
you as Commissioner, in respect of an allegation of perjury made by me as th=
e alleged victim in financial remedy proceedings BV20D01752.

The request is in three parts:=20

(i)                  that the allegation be recorded as a notifiable crime =
under the Home Office Counting Rules and the National Crime Recording Standa=
rd within 72 hours (seven days at the outer limit);=20

(ii)                that the matter be assessed on the facts under the fram=
ework set out in the published CPS Judicial Comments guidance; and=20

(iii)              that I be provided with a written reasoned response with=
in fourteen days.

The request is anchored in the published statutory and policy framework and=
 is supported by documentary evidence including extracts of the relevant SEC=
 filings (CIK 1852973), the two signatures by Mr Zahmoul on successive Regis=
tration Statement amendments dated 5 and 11 January 2024, the SEC Form 8-K o=
f 5 February 2024 reporting the Oxus Extraordinary General Meeting of 2 Febr=
uary 2024 at which shareholders approved the Business Combination, a chronol=
ogical timeline of the documentary contradiction, the Applicant's annotated =
153-page SEC filings index, and the public-record statement of even date whi=
ch sets out the full factual and legal basis. The Applicant's correspondence=
 with the Metropolitan Police Service Directorate of Professional Standards =
on 8 May 2026 is addressed in the supporting documents and quoted in full at=
 section 5(a) of the formal request.

This is a supplementary submission to the existing Metropolitan Police crim=
inal referral file CCR-6501-26-0100-000, operational engagement recorded 28 =
April 2026.

Respectfully,

Nadia Zahmoul Litigant in Person | BV20D01752 | Veritas Numquam Perit

=20

Attachments:
Formal Request MPS Commissioner 19May2026
Day5 Public Record 19May2026
Day5 Exhibit 34DaySequence 19May2026
SEC Filings Excerpts CIK1852973
Day5 Exhibit 6March2024 Email to Judge
Exhibit NZ1 SEC Filings Index
D11 Application Notice OXUS False Representations 7March2024
=20

=20

